# tug-provider-[[.Name]]

A [tug](https://github.com/paingha/tugcli) provider plugin for [[.Name]].

## Develop

```bash
make test          # unit tests
make link          # build and let tug use this directory
make conformance   # run tug's protocol conformance suite against it
tug import [[.Name]] --account demo --set clusters=dev=https://127.0.0.1:6443
```

The plugin is an executable that reads one JSON request on stdin and writes
one JSON response on stdout; `provider.Main` handles that. Implement `List`
and `Credential` in `main.go` with calls to your provider's API.

## Release

`make package` builds every platform in `plugin.yaml` and writes
`dist/tug-provider-[[.Name]]_<version>.tar.gz`, recording each binary's sha256
in the packaged manifest. Users install it with:

```bash
tug plugin install <url or file> --sha256 <archive sha256>
```

Pushing a `v*` tag runs `.github/workflows/release.yml`, which does this and
attaches the archive to a GitHub release.
